  {
    "__type__": "cc.Label",
    "_name": "",
    "_objFlags": 0,
    "node": {
      "__id__": 556
    },
    "_enabled": false,
    "_materials": [
      {
        "__uuid__": "eca5d2f2-8ef6-41c2-bbe6-f9c79d09c432"
      }
    ],
    "_srcBlendFactor": 770,
    "_dstBlendFactor": 771,
    "_string": "1.The game is played with 52 playing cards. At the beginning of each round, three cards are dealt to \"Ice Cream\", \"Pastry\" and \"Beer\".\n\n2.Players may wager on which of \"Ice Cream,\" \"Pastry,\" or \"Beer\" possesses the most formidable card combination, with the victorious gambler receiving a reward of X3 times their wagered coins.\n\n3.In each round, players can only bet on two of the three players, and can also join the \"Crown\" betting.\n\n4.\"Crown\" Guess:  If the winning side among \"Ice Cream,\" \"Pastries,\" or \"Beer\" features any of the following poker hands – FLUSH, STRAIGHT, STRAIGHT FLUSH, or THREE OF A KIND – in their card combination, the player will be granted a prize based on the highest multiplier corresponding to that particular hand.\n\n5.Hand Descriptions:\n-Hand Rankings: Three of a Kind > Straight Flush > Straight > Flush > Pair > High Card.\n-In the event of identical hand types, the hand with the higher-ranking cards wins: A > K > Q > J > 10 > 9 > 8 > 7 > 6 > 5 > 4 > 3 > 2.\n-When hand types and point values are equal, suits are arranged in descending order: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds.",
    "_N$string": "1.The game is played with 52 playing cards. At the beginning of each round, three cards are dealt to \"Ice Cream\", \"Pastry\" and \"Beer\".\n\n2.Players may wager on which of \"Ice Cream,\" \"Pastry,\" or \"Beer\" possesses the most formidable card combination, with the victorious gambler receiving a reward of X3 times their wagered coins.\n\n3.In each round, players can only bet on two of the three players, and can also join the \"Crown\" betting.\n\n4.\"Crown\" Guess:  If the winning side among \"Ice Cream,\" \"Pastries,\" or \"Beer\" features any of the following poker hands – FLUSH, STRAIGHT, STRAIGHT FLUSH, or THREE OF A KIND – in their card combination, the player will be granted a prize based on the highest multiplier corresponding to that particular hand.\n\n5.Hand Descriptions:\n-Hand Rankings: Three of a Kind > Straight Flush > Straight > Flush > Pair > High Card.\n-In the event of identical hand types, the hand with the higher-ranking cards wins: A > K > Q > J > 10 > 9 > 8 > 7 > 6 > 5 > 4 > 3 > 2.\n-When hand types and point values are equal, suits are arranged in descending order: Spades > Hearts > Clubs > Diamonds.",
    "_fontSize": 40,
    "_lineHeight": 40,
    "_enableWrapText": true,
    "_N$file": null,
